## 58. Length of Last Word

# Approach — Traverse From Right
--  Start from the last index of the string using s.length() - 1.
--  First, check for any trailing spaces.
--  If there are spaces, keep moving backward until we reach the last word.
--  Once we reach a character, start counting the characters.
--  Keep moving backward and increment count until we encounter a space.
--  When a space is found, the last word has ended.
--  Return count.

## Example
For:

" fly me to the moon "

Start from right
        ↓
"   fly me   to   the moon  "
                          ↑
                    skip spaces
                          ↓
"   fly me   to   the moon"
                       ↑
                  count backward
                       ↓
                    "moon"

count = 4

## Complexity
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
Approach: Optimal

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLastWord(String s) {
        int i = s.length() - 1;
        int count = 0;
        while (s.charAt(i) == ' ') {
            i--;
        }
        while (i >= 0 && s.charAt(i) != ' ') {
            count++;
            i--;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
